     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "nhé and đi (polite commands and suggestions)",
     "texto": [
      "**đi** at the end turns the sentence into a command or a «come on!»: **Thức dậy đi!** = Get up!",
      "**nhé** at the end is softer, like «OK?»: it is used to suggest or ask for something, and it is better with older people: **Đi ăn phở với tôi nhé** = let's go and eat phở, OK?",
      "It is also used when thanking: **Cảm ơn nhé!**",
      "Important! Without **đi** or **nhé**, a command sounds abrupt and bossy."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking politely: xin + person + verb",
     "texto": [
      "**xin** at the start = «please». It is the most polite way to ask for something, perfect with older family members.",
      "**Xin ông nói chậm.** = Please speak slowly. · **Xin cô nói lại.** = Please repeat.",
      "**xin mời** = to invite politely: **Xin mời bà vào.** = Come in, madam. · **Xin mời ông ngồi.** = Please, have a seat.",
      "**Tôi xin giới thiệu…** = Let me introduce… · **Tôi xin tự giới thiệu** = Allow me to introduce myself.",
      "• Adding **ạ** at the end makes it even more respectful: **Xin bà nói chậm ạ.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
